    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1185">

                <pb facs="1432" n="1418" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg1418"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 EW/1–1645: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Venezuela</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-01-16T17:00:00-04:30">January 16, 1945—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:19 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>31. Reference Department’s 21, January 12, 3 p.m.<anchor n="32" xml:id="d1185-f1"
                    /> I had a conversation with the Foreign Minister<anchor n="33"
                        xml:id="d1185-f2"/> this morning which lasted over an hour and will be
                    resumed tomorrow after he has talked to President Medina.<anchor n="34"
                        xml:id="d1185-f3"/> Preliminary reaction not unfavorable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1185-f1" n="32" xml:id="d1185-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram 43, January 12, 3 p.m., to Lima, and footnote 1, <ref
                        target="#pg1312">p. 1312</ref>. The telegram pointed out the possibility
                    that those nations not in a state of war with the Axis might not have the
                    opportunity to join the United Nations or participate in the post-war
                    deliberations.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1185-f2" n="33" xml:id="d1185-f2-content">
                <p>Caracciolo Parra-Perez.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1185-f3" n="34" xml:id="d1185-f3-content">
                <p>Gen. Isaias Medina Angarita.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
